  "notes": "Example data only; enter your fabricator's current values. Read 2026-10-13 from the JLCPCB capabilities page and one help article through a summarizing fetcher (several narrow fetches that agreed), not a browser: re-read in a browser before use (R-21). Fabricators change limits without notice. All values are UNVERIFIED (single publisher, ledger rows S-019i..S-019m; S-019c for finished copper). Each limit sits in scopedLimits with its own hole type, layer count, copper weight and layer side: a lookup returns only the exact scope, or 'not published' / 'not available'; nothing is borrowed from another scope. The old flat keys (one holeToTrack, drillTolerance, minAnnularRing and others) were removed because they mixed scopes and one was misnamed. Scope notes: the ring rows are 'PTH annular ring' and 'NPTH pad annular ring'; there is no via ring row (only a via pad-minus-hole rule). The through-hole tolerance +0.13/-0.08 mm is a finished-hole tolerance for plated pad holes; vias are 'not controlled' and round non-plated holes are not published. 'Average' plating (18 um) is not a minimum. Trace/space for 1 oz multilayer is stored as the published 0.09 mm (3.5 mil = 0.0889 mm is smaller). Not published by the fabricator, so absent: minimum plating thickness, aspect ratio, pad size tolerance, layer-to-layer registration, etch compensation, drill-bit oversize over the finished hole, whether the ring and hole-to-track limits are measured from the finished or the drill hole, inner versus outer split of most rows. Finished copper (S-019c, UNVERIFIED, read 2026-10-13 from the multilayer stackup article): outer 1 oz 1.6 mil, inner 0.5 oz 0.6 mil, inner 1 oz 1.2 mil; the label-to-value pairing is by order from a flattened table and is unconfirmed; it is not stated whether 1.6 mil includes plating; do not compare with IPC-6012 minimums without checking the basis. Same-publisher conflict not resolved: the 2025-04-24 help article says only through-hole vias are offered; the capabilities page lists blind and buried vias (out of scope).",
